+{
+  "sample": true,
+  "diagnosis": "You have a credible reason to reconnect because the customer supplied real scheduling information and still faces a complex coordination decision. The strongest outreach helps them compare sequencing tradeoffs without asking them to restart the full sales conversation.",
+  "assumptions": ["Fictional sample: Prairie Air Systems has permission to follow up on the proposal.", "The maintenance-window dates are verified but no installation slot is reserved."],
+  "plays": [
+    {
+      "rank": 1, "title": "Six-site sequencing map", "strategicAngle": "Turn the new maintenance windows into a practical decision aid.", "whyNow": "The customer can evaluate disruption before peak cooling demand narrows its options.", "valueToBring": "Create a one-page draft that compares two phased sequences; label dates and assumptions for confirmation.", "primaryChannel": "Email", "sequence": ["Email the draft map and name the assumptions.", "Offer a 15-minute correction session four business days later.", "Close the loop after one follow-up."], "rationale": "Highly relevant and useful because it converts verified timing into decision help without manufacturing urgency.",
+      "rubric": {"relevance":2,"newness":2,"value":2,"decisionHelp":2,"prospectBenefit":2,"total":10},
+      "scripts": {
+        "Email": "Subject: A draft sequence for the six locations\n\nHi Jordan,\n\nYou shared the summer maintenance windows, so I mapped two possible ways to phase the six rooftop-unit replacements. It is a draft—not a reserved schedule—and I marked the assumptions that need your correction. If it would save your team time, I can send the one-page comparison before we discuss anything else.\n\nAvery",
+        "Call opener": "Hi Jordan, this is Avery. I used the maintenance windows you shared to sketch two ways the six replacements could be phased. Nothing is reserved; I wanted to see whether comparing the disruption points would be useful. Do you have a minute for the headline?\n\nAvery",
+        "Voicemail": "Hi Jordan, this is Avery. I mapped two possible sequences around the maintenance windows you shared and flagged the assumptions. I’ll email the one-page draft so you can decide whether it is useful.\n\nAvery",
+        "Text": "Hi Jordan—Avery here. I drafted two ways to phase the six sites around the windows you shared. Nothing is reserved. Would the one-page comparison be useful?\n\nAvery",
+        "LinkedIn": "Hi Jordan, I turned the maintenance windows you shared into a draft two-option sequencing map for the six sites. I marked every assumption. Happy to send it if comparing disruption points would help.\n\nAvery",
+        "Mailed card": "Hi Jordan,\n\nThank you for sharing the maintenance windows. I drafted two possible sequences for the six sites and marked what still needs your correction. If comparing the disruption points would help, I’m glad to send it.\n\nAvery",
+        "Gift/leave-behind": "Hi Jordan,\n\nI created this simple six-site sequencing worksheet around the maintenance windows you shared. It is only a draft, with assumptions clearly marked. I hope it makes the tradeoffs easier to review.\n\nAvery"
+      }
+    },
+    {
+      "rank": 2, "title": "Downtime assumption check", "strategicAngle": "Invite correction of the three assumptions most likely to change the recommendation.", "whyNow": "Confirming operating constraints can prevent both teams from optimizing the wrong installation sequence.", "valueToBring": "Prepare three concise assumptions about access, peak hours, and acceptable overlap.", "primaryChannel": "Call opener", "sequence": ["Call with three assumptions.", "Send the corrected list after the call."], "rationale": "Specific and low effort, though less tangible than the full sequencing map.",
+      "rubric": {"relevance":2,"newness":2,"value":1,"decisionHelp":2,"prospectBenefit":2,"total":9},
+      "scripts": {"Email":"Subject: Three assumptions to correct\n\nHi Jordan,\n\nBefore we revise the proposal, I wrote down three assumptions about site access, peak operating hours, and acceptable overlap. A quick correction would help us avoid recommending a sequence that creates more disruption. May I send the short list?\n\nAvery","Call opener":"Hi Jordan, this is Avery. I wrote down three assumptions that could materially change the six-site sequence. Could I read them to you in under a minute so you can tell me where we are wrong?\n\nAvery","Voicemail":"Hi Jordan, this is Avery. I have three short assumptions about access and downtime that could change our recommendation. I’ll send them so you can correct anything that is off.\n\nAvery","Text":"Hi Jordan—Avery here. I have three assumptions about site access and downtime that could change the sequence. May I send the short list for correction?\n\nAvery","LinkedIn":"Hi Jordan, I captured three assumptions about access, peak hours, and acceptable overlap. Correcting them may be the fastest way to improve the proposed sequence. Happy to send the short list.\n\nAvery","Mailed card":"Hi Jordan,\n\nI wrote down three assumptions that could change the six-site sequence. I would rather invite your correction than fill in the gaps. I’m happy to send the short list whenever useful.\n\nAvery","Gift/leave-behind":"Hi Jordan,\n\nThis small assumption-check sheet covers the three operating constraints most likely to affect sequencing. I hope it saves your team time; there is no expectation attached.\n\nAvery"}
+    },
+    {
+      "rank": 3, "title": "Peak-season risk review", "strategicAngle": "Focus a short conversation on one decision: which site cannot tolerate overlap.", "whyNow": "Identifying the least flexible site can simplify the rest of the phasing decision.", "valueToBring": "Create a 15-minute agenda with one prioritization question and a clear stopping point.", "primaryChannel": "Text", "sequence": ["Text the single decision question.", "Offer the short agenda if the question is relevant."], "rationale": "Useful and bounded, but depends on the customer wanting a live conversation.",
+      "rubric": {"relevance":2,"newness":1,"value":1,"decisionHelp":2,"prospectBenefit":2,"total":8},
+      "scripts": {"Email":"Subject: One sequencing question\n\nHi Jordan,\n\nWhich of the six sites has the least tolerance for installation overlap? That answer may simplify the entire sequence. If useful, I can bring a 15-minute agenda focused only on that decision.\n\nAvery","Call opener":"Hi Jordan, this is Avery. I have one question that may simplify the six-site sequence: which location has the least tolerance for overlap? Is now a reasonable time to test that assumption?\n\nAvery","Voicemail":"Hi Jordan, this is Avery. One prioritization question may simplify the full sequence. I’ll send it by text; if it is useful, we can keep the conversation to 15 minutes.\n\nAvery","Text":"Hi Jordan—Avery here. Which of the six sites has the least tolerance for installation overlap? That may simplify the sequence. Worth a focused 15-minute review?\n\nAvery","LinkedIn":"Hi Jordan, one question may simplify the six-site plan: which location has the least tolerance for overlap? I can share a focused 15-minute review agenda if helpful.\n\nAvery","Mailed card":"Hi Jordan,\n\nOne question may simplify the full sequence: which site has the least tolerance for installation overlap? If useful, I can keep a review focused only on that decision.\n\nAvery","Gift/leave-behind":"Hi Jordan,\n\nThis simple priority card is meant to help identify the least flexible site first. I hope it makes the broader sequence easier to evaluate.\n\nAvery"}
+    },
+    {
+      "rank": 4, "title": "Useful pause with a checkpoint", "strategicAngle": "Give the customer control over timing while leaving a concrete re-entry point.", "whyNow": "A respectful pause protects the relationship if internal comparison work is still underway.", "valueToBring": "Summarize the verified window dates and the one open sequencing question in a concise recap.", "primaryChannel": "Mailed card", "sequence": ["Mail the concise recap.", "Pause unless the customer responds or the agreed checkpoint arrives."], "rationale": "Respectful and low pressure, though it provides less immediate decision help than the top plays.",
+      "rubric": {"relevance":2,"newness":1,"value":1,"decisionHelp":1,"prospectBenefit":2,"total":7},
+      "scripts": {"Email":"Subject: A clean checkpoint\n\nHi Jordan,\n\nI know your team is still comparing options. I summarized the maintenance windows you shared and the one sequencing question that remains open. I’m happy to send it, then leave timing with you.\n\nAvery","Call opener":"Hi Jordan, this is Avery. I don’t want to add noise while your team compares options. I prepared a concise recap of the verified windows and one open sequencing question. Would that be useful before I step back?\n\nAvery","Voicemail":"Hi Jordan, this is Avery. I prepared a concise recap of the maintenance windows and one open sequencing question. I’ll send a short note, then leave the timing with you.\n\nAvery","Text":"Hi Jordan—Avery here. I summarized the verified windows and one open sequencing question. Would the short recap help while your team compares options?\n\nAvery","LinkedIn":"Hi Jordan, I prepared a concise recap of the verified maintenance windows and one remaining sequencing question. Happy to share it, then leave timing with you.\n\nAvery","Mailed card":"Hi Jordan,\n\nI know your team is comparing options, so I wanted to leave a clean recap rather than another follow-up request. I noted the maintenance windows you shared and the one sequencing question still open. I’m happy to help when the timing is useful.\n\nAvery","Gift/leave-behind":"Hi Jordan,\n\nThis concise checkpoint captures the verified maintenance windows and the one sequencing question still open. I hope it is useful while your team compares options; there is no expectation attached.\n\nAvery"}
+    }
+  ]
+}
